<h2>Practical Tips for Gangnam</h2>
<p><strong>Best time to visit:</strong> Gangnam is pleasant year-round. Garosu-gil is especially beautiful in autumn (October–November) when the ginkgo trees turn golden. Avoid the area on weekends if you hate crowds — COEX gets genuinely packed.</p>
<p><strong>Budget:</strong> Gangnam is Seoul's most expensive neighborhood but still affordable by international standards. A nice lunch at a sit-down restaurant runs ₩15,000–30,000. Coffee at a specialty café costs ₩6,000–8,000.</p>
<p><strong>Language:</strong> English is more widely spoken here than in other parts of Seoul, particularly in hotels, restaurants, and retail shops in the COEX area.</p>

